  "comment": "Property-schema update fields: `propertySchema.update` gains `icon`, `scopeClassIds`, `targetClassFilter`, `multi`, and `validationRules` ({min?, max?, pattern} — min/max on number schemas, pattern on text/email, min <= max), all nullable with the keep/clear contract (absent keeps the stored value, present-null clears). This fixture exercises the full set/clear lifecycle on a scratch workspace: a global 'Score' number schema gains an icon, multi, and {min: 0, max: 10} rules (an absent-field update keeps them), then clears all three back to defaults; an object-typed 'Related' schema gains a targetClassFilter and a scopeClassIds list, then clears both. The store suite asserts the column values through the lifecycle. (The reject shapes — the retired `scope` key, an empty scopeClassIds, min > max, min on a text schema — are parse-level strict-schema rejects pinned in the protocol suite; applicability against the stored type is pinned in the store suite.) LOCKSTEP-PENDING: GTK/Flutter validators/appliers converge before the live migration runs.",
